 "notes": "A long, narrow hole of white sand at 15-20 m in the reef slope seaward of the Lac Bay barrier reef (reef top 4-6 m, 30 m at most on the outside), home to a resting school of tarpon that shelter in the coral wall on its west side, with turtles on the southern part (bonaire.com, bonaireisland.com). The sand hole is about 140 m long and 25 m wide, beside the OpenStreetMap dive-site marker; the 30 m contour, the drop point and the circular route are assumptions. Coastline and reef outline © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Positions are approximate.",
